    "id": "guard_app_onboarding.txt-0",
    "document": "guard_app_onboarding.txt",
    "section": "General",
    "text": "SecureShift Guard App onboarding - current handover\nThe root README.md is the canonical full-stack quickstart; guard_app/README.md\ncovers mobile development. Earlier version 1.0 instructions are superseded.\nThis is one monorepo: app-backend, app-frontend/employer-panel,\napp-frontend/admin-panel, and guard_app. The mobile app runs outside Compose.\n1. Backend and local services\nUse Docker with Compose. From the repository root, on first setup:\ndocker compose up --build -d\ndocker compose ps -a\ndocker compose logs ollama-models ai-indexer\nNo private credentials or backend .env are required for ordinary local Compose.\nAll eight services: backend, mongodb, mailpit, frontend-employer, frontend-admin,\nollama, ollama-models, ai-indexer. The last two are one-shot jobs; Exited (0)\nmeans success.\nAfter successful indexing, ensure the backend loads the regenerated vectors:\nIf the backend is already running:\ndocker compose restart backend\nIf the backend is not currently running:\ndocker compose up -d backend\nBackend: http://localhost:5000/api/v1/health\nSwagger: http://localhost:5000/api-docs\nEmployer panel: http://localhost:3000\nAdmin panel: http://localhost:3001\nMongoDB: localhost:27017\nMailpit SMTP: localhost:1025; inbox: http://localhost:8025\nUse BACKEND_HOST_PORT=5001 in the optional root .env if port 5000 is occupied,\nand adjust client URLs. No volume reset is needed for a fresh clone.\n2. AI readiness\nModels: nomic-embed-text:latest and llama3.2:latest. Compose Ollama is not\npublished to the host. Host AI requires a separately reachable Ollama server.\nBackend HTTP 200 does not guarantee AI/index readiness; the backend does not\nwait for indexing and loads vectors at startup. All three indexed TXT sources\nin app-backend/knowledge-base/docs are backend_onboarding_v1.1.txt,\nonboarding.txt, and guard_app_onboarding.txt. After source changes, run:\ndocker compose run --rm ai-indexer",
