    "section": "General",
    "text": "General\nAfter successful indexing, ensure the backend loads the regenerated vectors:\nIf the backend is already running:\ndocker compose restart backend\nIf the backend is not currently running:\ndocker compose up -d backend\nRegeneration for this documentation cleanup is deferred until review.\n3. Run the Guard App\nGuard App mobile tooling requires Node >=20.19.4. Node 22.13+ is compatible and\na convenient shared local version for backend development; the backend requires\nNode >=22.13.0. Use npm and Expo Go on your phone, or Android Studio / Xcode\nfor an emulator or simulator. From the root:\ncd guard_app\nnpm ci\nnpm start\nSelect Expo Go (press s if needed), then scan the QR code. Alternatives, run\nseparately: npm run android, npm run ios (macOS), npm run web.\nSet guard_app/.env to a reachable backend address for your device, for example:\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:5000\nReplace the IP with your computer's LAN address. Android emulator can use\nhttp://10.0.2.2:5000. Use 5001 if configured. Do not append /api/v1; the app adds\nit. Restart Expo after environment changes. Physical devices need network\naccess; check host/WSL forwarding and firewalls if connection fails.\n4. Accounts and email\nUse local fixtures documented in app-backend/README.md or register a guard and\nfollow the approval flow. Sign out of any previous session to use another account.\nEmployer and guard OTP messages are captured by Mailpit at http://localhost:8025\non your computer. No private SMTP credentials are required. Disabling email does\nnot expose an OTP fallback. Normal seed and destructive reset commands are",
