    "section": "General",
    "text": "General\nseparate in the backend README; reset is not an onboarding step.\n5. Daily development\nFrom the repository root:\ndocker compose up -d\ndocker compose ps -a\nAfter successful indexing, use the restart/start commands in section 2 to load\nregenerated vectors. Run npm start from guard_app.\nNormal shutdown preserves data, models, and uploads:\ndocker compose down\nWARNING: docker compose down -v deletes MongoDB data, downloaded Ollama models,\nand uploads. It is not routine cleanup.\nFor a host backend, follow ENVIRONMENT_SETUP.md: Node >=22.13.0, npm ci, MongoDB\nand Mailpit in Compose. Runtime validation was recorded at Node v22.13.1;\nbackend npm run test:ci covered 5 suites, 91/91 passing in the handover snapshot.\nGuard App checks: npm run lint, npm run typecheck, npm run test:ci.\nConfirm the team's current branch/PR target before contributing.",
